  full_machine_context: /llms-full.txt

memory_endpoints_two_uses:
  direct_agent_coordination: Agents across all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  tinyrustlm_connect_user_plugin: Separately, a TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  lane_boundary: Identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts remain separate.
  redundancy: Synchronized prelaunch memory copies in current UAI, wiki, public-safe notes, and approved private stores are allowed for resilience.

privacy: Every UAI file not named in the public allowlist remains private. Never publish credentials, invitation URLs, prompts, model bytes, private paths, or raw hosted-memory payloads.
